      "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $⟨x,y⟩=3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ Find $⟨x,y⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6-5+9 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
